{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE — fix landed as Gerrit change 2142, merged to main as\n1a2b59ea912d568fb9eed0c3adc1c8fdc6825d55 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1,\n0 unresolved comments).\n\nFix (per the d70a contract): the sign fence in\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py is scoped to the SUBJECT'S\nGENERATION. The store-wide head samples (`before`/`after` around collect,\n`locked_head` under lock) are DELETED; the sole authoritative pre-sign\ncheck is the under-lock re-collect compared against the immutable initial\nbaseline. Site C: relation_snapshot's strict status read now classifies a\npeer writer's index-only staged entry (clean worktree column) as\nnon-dirt via `_status_line_is_dirt` (unmerged XY / untracked / worktree\nmodifications remain fatal). Patchset 2 additionally routes a transient\nstore-read-failure raised by the UNDER-LOCK re-collect through the same\nbounded jittered retry as the pre-lock read (LLM-Review blocking finding);\ndeterministic reasons stay terminal.\n\nPer-AC evidence (all tests merged in change 2142; CI green on\npy3.11/3.12/3.13 ubuntu + macos):\n- AC-1 unrelated commits mid-attempt: test_signs_while_unrelated_commits_land_mid_attempt\n  (real temp git tracker, unrelated events committed between reads) — PASS.\n- AC-2 unrelated commit during lock acquisition:\n  test_signs_when_unrelated_commit_lands_during_lock_acquisition — PASS.\n- AC-3 genuine drift fails closed named: subject/related drift tests assert\n  PlanReviewGenerationChanged with the changed component named — PASS.\n- AC-4 staged-index tolerance: test_tracker_head_sha_tolerates_peer_staged_index,\n  test_tracker_head_sha_still_fails_on_dirty_tracked_worktree, and\n  test_status_line_unmerged_entries_are_dirt — PASS.\n- AC-5 named under-lock reason: test_under_lock_generation_drift_retries_named_then_exhausts\n  asserts reason=\"generation-drift-under-lock\" on every retry — PASS.\n- AC-6 scope tests no longer freeze tracker_head_sha:\n  test_plan_review_generation_scope.py rewritten on a real git tracker\n  fixture with zero tracker_head_sha/config monkeypatching — PASS.\n- AC-7 stuck-ticket recovery, run with the FIXED build (head 1a2b59ea91)\n  against the live busy store:\n  * 111a-4626-8d2c-42bf — sign-review OK, signed=true, head_sha 1a2b59ea91.\n  * 7931-faee-53ba-47b1 — sign-review OK, signed=true, head_sha 1a2b59ea91.\n  * 825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f — no longer starved: fails closed with the NAMED\n    terminal reason \"the plan changed since the review — changed:\n    description (4935 -> 7995 chars)\" (its description genuinely changed\n    after its review), i.e. the fix converts starvation into an actionable\n    verdict; a fresh `rebar review-plan 825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f` was started to\n    restore its attestation.\n\nValidation at merge: targeted suites green (38/38 across\ntest_plan_review_sign_transaction / test_plan_relation_snapshot /\ntest_plan_review_generation_scope), make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS\n(638 files), complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0 (sign_manifest got\nsimpler; stale entries left untouched per policy).\n\ncaused_by: d70a-d06e-aea0-4008 (the fence contract's implementation\ndiverged from its documented subject-generation scope — plan_defect /\nincomplete implementation; caused_by link already recorded)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787456146779837001,"uuid":"60b2642e-94e2-439c-bdf5-3cb7cf38cdf0"}